# Vite Configuration:

- Import `path` from Node.js for path resolution.
- Use `@vitejs/plugin-react` for React support.
- Use `@tailwindcss/vite` for Tailwind CSS integration.
- Configure `resolve.alias` with `@` mapping to `./src`.
- Set proper build options for component library usage.

TypeScript Configuration:

- Configure `baseUrl: "."` in `tsconfig.json` and `tsconfig.app.json`.
- Set `paths: { "@/*": ["./src/*"] }` for absolute imports.
- Enable strict TypeScript options for type safety.
- Configure proper module resolution for component imports.
- Set `jsx: "react-jsx"` for modern React syntax.

Path Resolution:

- Use `path.resolve(__dirname, "./src")` for alias configuration.
- Ensure consistent path mapping across all config files.
- Configure proper module resolution for component discovery.
- Set up proper import alias resolution for development.
- Use absolute paths for component imports.

Build Optimization:

- Configure proper chunk splitting for component libraries.
- Set up tree shaking for unused component removal.
- Optimize bundle size with proper dependency management.
- Configure proper source maps for debugging.
- Set up proper asset handling for component resources.

Development Setup:

- Install `@types/node` for Node.js type definitions.
- Configure proper hot module replacement for components.
- Set up proper development server configuration.
- Configure proper environment variable handling.
- Set up proper proxy configuration if needed.

Production Build:

- Configure proper minification for production builds.
- Set up proper asset optimization for component resources.
- Configure proper chunk naming for better caching.
- Set up proper source map generation for debugging.
- Configure proper build output directory structure.

Dependencies:

- Install `tailwindcss` and `@tailwindcss/vite` for styling.
- Install `@vitejs/plugin-react` for React support.
- Install `@types/node` for TypeScript support.
- Install `class-variance-authority` for component variants.
- Install `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for class utilities.

Configuration Validation:

- Verify path aliases work correctly in development.
- Test component imports with configured aliases.
- Validate TypeScript path resolution in IDE.
- Test build process with component library.
- Verify proper asset loading in development and production.
